age>1683</fpage><lpage>1688</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12829633</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001071-Mabley1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mabley</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Jagtap</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Perretti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Getting</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Salzman</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Anti-inflammatory effects of a novel, potent inhibitor of poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase.</article-title><source>Inflamm Res</source><volume>50</volume><fpage>561</fpage><lpage>569</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11766996</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001071-Scott2"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kean</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mikheeva</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Fabis</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mabley</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The therapeutic effects of PJ34 &#x0005b;N-(6-oxo-5,6-dihydrophenanthridin-2-yl)-N,N-dimethylacetamide.HCl&#x0005d;, a selective inhibitor of poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase, in experimental allergic encephalomyelitis are associated with immunomodulation.</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><volume>310</volume><fpage>1053</fpage><lpage>1061</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15159442</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001071-Pascual1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pascual</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lopez-Nevot</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Caliz</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrer</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Balsa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase haplotype spanning the promoter region confers susceptibility to rheumatoid arthritis.</article-title><source>Arthritis Rheum</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>638</fpage><lpage>641</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12632415</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001071-Hur1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hur</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Sung</surname><given-names>YK</given-names></name><name><surname>Shin</surname><given-names>HD</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheong</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) polymorphisms associated with nephritis and arthritis in systemic lupus erythematosus.</article-title><source>Rheumatology (Oxford)</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>711</fpage><lpage>717</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16461442</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001071-1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Di Paola</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Genovese</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Caputi</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Threadgill</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thiemermann</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Beneficial effects of 5-aminoisoquinolinone, a novel, potent, water-soluble, inhibitor of poly (ADP-ribose) poly